==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|lesa}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*lesaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlɛːsa/|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|ɛːsa|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|las|lásu|lesið}}

# {{lb|is|ambitransitive|with accusative}} to [[read]]
#: ''Ég er að '''lesa''' bók um forritun.''
#:: I'm '''reading''' a book on programming.
#: ''Þá var bréfið '''lesið''' upphátt fyrir allan bekkinn.''
#:: The letter was then '''read''' aloud in front of the entire class.
# {{lb|is|ambitransitive|with accusative}} to [[study]]
# {{lb|is|transitive|with accusative}} to [[gather]], [[pick]] (usually berries, etc.)

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-s5|l|e|s|mp=-}}

====Derived terms====
{{der-top}}
* {{l|is|lesa fyrir bréf}} (to dictate a letter)
* {{l|is|lesa saman}} (to compare)
* {{l|is|lesa spjaldanna á milli}}
* {{l|is|lesa upphátt}} (to read aloud)
{{der-mid}}
* {{l|is|lesa upp}} (to recite)
* {{l|is|lesblinda}}
* {{l|is|lesblindur}}
* {{l|is|les-}} ([[read-only]])
{{der-bottom}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|is|lestur}}

