==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*lesaną}}. The sense “read” is derived from West Germanic (Old Saxon or Old High German), calquing {{cog|la|legō||gather, read}}; for reading the Germanic [[rune]]s, which were in use before the adoption of the Latin alphabet, the usual verb had been {{m|non|ráða}} (same as English {{m|en|read}}).

===Verb===
{{non-verb}}

# to [[gather]], [[pick]]
# to [[read]]

====Descendants====
* Icelandic: {{l|is|lesa}}
* Faroese: {{l|fo|lesa}}
* Norwegian: {{l|no|lese}}
* Danish: {{l|da|læse}}
* Swedish: {{l|sv|läsa}}

